.TH MC1-HEALTHCHECK 1 "2026-10-28" "mu2edaq-batch-queues" "Mu2e DAQ Tools"
.SH NAME
mc1-healthcheck \- Slurm health checks for the MC1 cluster, with a status web site and mail on problems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mc1-healthcheck
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-\-set
.IR key=value ]...
.RB [ \-q ]
.B run
.RB [ \-\-only
.IR check[,check...] ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-mail ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-web ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B mc1-healthcheck
.RI [ options ]
.BR render " | " mail\-test " [" \-\-to
.IR addr ]
.RB " | " list " | " config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mc1-healthcheck
runs on the Slurm controller,
.BR mu2e-mc1-worker-01 ,
from the crontab of the job account
.B mu2ebatch
(every 30 minutes by default). Each run:
.IP 1. 3
runs the checks below as the invoking user. They only read state or submit
small jobs named
.BR mc1hc\-* ;
nothing is restarted, drained or rebooted;
.IP 2.
writes
.I status.json
and
.I history.json
to the state directory and, with the HTML pages, to the web directory served by
httpd on the controller to loopback clients;
.IP 3.
mails
.B mail.to
when the overall state turns bad, when the set of failing checks changes, every
.B mail.reminder_hours
while it stays bad, and once when it recovers.
.PP
A run that finds another run still in progress (lock
.IR <state_dir>/run.lock )
exits with status 4 without doing anything.
.SH CHECKS
.TP
.B controller_services
.BR "systemctl is-active" " of slurmctld, slurmdbd, mariadb, munge and"
.BR mc1-fw-zone-guard.timer ,
and the last result of
.BR mc1-fw-zone-guard.service .
.TP
.B controller_ping
.B scontrol ping
reports slurmctld UP. If not, the node and job checks are skipped.
.TP
.B controller_disk
Free space on each path in
.B controller_paths
(GiB); below the minimum is a warning.
.TP
.B accounting
.B sacctmgr
answers and the running user has an association. Without one,
.B AccountingStorageEnforce
rejects the user's jobs.
.TP
.B node_states
.BR sinfo :
each node in
.B expected_nodes
is idle, mixed or allocated. Drained is a warning; down, not responding
.RB ( * )
or absent is a failure. Only usable nodes take part in the job checks.
.TP
.B node_probe
One
.B srun
across every usable node, reported as five checks:
.B node_srun
(the node ran the task),
.B node_storage
(each
.B node_paths
entry writable, free space above its minimum),
.B node_cvmfs
(each repository lists),
.B node_ctld_port
(TCP connect to slurmctld) and
.B node_zone_guard
(the D24 timer is active).
.TP
.B sbatch_roundtrip
.B sbatch \-\-wait
of a one-node job, then
.B sacct
shows COMPLETED.
.TP
.B memory_limit
A 64 MB job that allocates 512 MB must be killed by the cgroup limit.
.TP
.B cpu_binding
.B srun \-c2 nproc
prints 2.
.TP
.B job_array
A 4-task array; all COMPLETED in
.BR sacct .
.PP
.B memory_limit
and
.B cpu_binding
use one node per run, rotating hourly, so every node is covered within a day.
If the cluster is full,
.B srun \-\-immediate
gives up after
.B srun_immediate
seconds. The check is then a warning ("cluster busy"), not a failure.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
(default) Run, write, mail.
.B \-\-only
limits the checks; controller_ping and node_states are added when a job check
needs them.
.B \-\-no\-mail
sends nothing, but the notification state is still updated.
.B \-\-no\-web
skips the web directory.
.B \-\-dry\-run
runs the checks, writes nothing, sends nothing, and prints the mail that would
go out.
.B \-\-json
prints status.json.
.TP
.B render
Rebuild the HTML from the saved status and history without running checks
(for example, after a template change).
.TP
.B mail\-test
Send a test message to
.B mail.to
or
.BR \-\-to .
.TP
.B list
The checks; enabled ones are marked *.
.TP
.B config
Print the effective configuration as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " file
YAML configuration. Env
.BR MC1_HC_CONFIG ;
default
.IR /etc/mc1-healthcheck/config.yaml .
.TP
.BI \-\-set " key=value"
Override any setting; nested keys use dots
.RB ( mail.enabled=false ,
.BR web.dir=/tmp/www ).
Values are parsed as YAML; list keys take comma-separated values.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print only when the result is not ok (used by cron).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Precedence: command line > environment > .env (next to the config file, then
the current directory) > config file > built-in defaults. Environment
variables:
.BR MC1_HC_CONFIG ,
.BR MC1_HC_PARTITION ,
.BR MC1_HC_CONTROLLER ,
.BR MC1_HC_EXPECTED_NODES ,
.BR MC1_HC_CHECKS ,
.BR MC1_HC_STATE_DIR ,
.BR MC1_HC_WEB_ENABLED ,
.BR MC1_HC_WEB_DIR ,
.BR MC1_HC_MAIL_ENABLED ,
.BR MC1_HC_MAIL_TO ,
.BR MC1_HC_MAIL_FROM ,
.BR MC1_HC_SMTP_HOST ,
.BR MC1_HC_NOTIFY_ON .
.PP
The deployed file is rendered by the Ansible role
.B healthcheck
from the
.B mc1_hc_*
variables in
.IR config/group_vars/all.yml .
Edit those and run
.BR "mc1-slurm-deploy healthcheck \-\-apply" .
.PP
.EX
cluster: mc1
partition: mc1
controller: mu2e-mc1-worker-01.fnal.gov
expected_nodes: [mu2e-mc1-worker-02, ..., mu2e-mc1-worker-18]
node_paths: {/scratch: 10, /data-local: 50}   # min free GiB
srun_immediate: 120                          # s to wait for free cores
state_dir: /var/lib/mc1-healthcheck
web: {dir: /var/www/mc1-status, history_runs: 336}
mail:
  to: [anorman@fnal.gov]
  notify_on: fail          # fail | warn
  reminder_hours: 12
  send_recovery: true
  smtp_host: ""            # empty = /usr/sbin/sendmail -t
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 ok, 1 warn, 2 fail, 3 the checks ran but results could not be written or mail
could not be sent (mail is retried on the next run), 4 another run is in
progress, 64 usage or configuration error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mc1-healthcheck/config.yaml
Configuration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/mc1-healthcheck/
.IR status.json ,
.IR history.json ,
.I notify.json
(mail decision state),
.IR run.lock ,
.I cron.log
(rotated weekly).
.TP
.I /var/www/mc1-status/
The site: index.html, history.html, api.html, about.html, sitemap.html,
status.json, history.json.
.TP
.I /etc/httpd/conf.d/mc1-status.conf
httpd site: loopback clients, plus the cluster members' addresses (Require ip) when
.B mc1_hc_web_cluster_access
is true; the firewall opens port 80 to the same members only.
.SH EXAMPLES
On the controller, as mu2ebatch:
.PP
.EX
mc1-healthcheck run --no-mail                 # full run, no mail
mc1-healthcheck run --only node_states,node_probe --no-web --no-mail
mc1-healthcheck run --dry-run                 # show the mail that would be sent
mc1-healthcheck mail-test                     # check the mail path
mc1-healthcheck --set mail.notify_on=warn run # mail on warnings this once
crontab -l                                    # the cron entry
tail /var/lib/mc1-healthcheck/cron.log
.EE
.PP
From any cluster node:
.PP
.EX
curl -s http://mu2e-mc1-worker-01.fnal.gov/status.json | python3 -m json.tool | head
.EE
.PP
From the operator machine:
.PP
.EX
scripts/mc1-status-tunnel -o                  # tunnel and open the browser
curl -s http://localhost:8081/status.json | jq .overall
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc1-status-tunnel (1),
.BR mc1-slurm-deploy (1),
.BR mc1-fw-zone-guard (8),
.BR sinfo (1),
.BR srun (1),
.BR crontab (5)
